index 971ab6f..8a7b32a 100644
--- a/notes/error-handling.md
+++ b/notes/error-handling.md
@@ -114,3 +114,33 @@ before surfacing the error.
 | `proto_tools/tools/tool_registry.py` | `_should_capture_errors()`, `PROTO_CAPTURE_ERRORS` env var, `_make_error_output_or_raise()` helper at the three exception sites in the `@tool` wrapper |
 | `proto_tools/utils/tool_io.py` | `MissingAssetError` (carve-out); `BaseToolOutput.success` / `BaseToolOutput.errors` capture-mode contract; `__getattr__` deferred raise on `success=False` outputs |
 | `tests/conftest.py` | Pytest hook that catches `MissingAssetError` and converts to skip |
+
+## Scoped request observation
+
+`proto_tools.utils.execution_observer.request_observation_scope(observer, control)`
+observes one complete public registry request, including normalized inputs/config,
+opaque request identity and parent identity, final output or escaping exception.
+Observer admission happens outside capture/retry machinery and may reject before
+effects. Returned `success=False` outputs are completed requests with failed
+output status. Observers must not mutate scientific inputs, config or outputs.
+
+The registry records `cache_hit`, `cache_partial`, `cache_miss`, `cache_disabled`,
+or `external_dispatch_backend` from the actual executed branch. These describe
+registered requests, not physical inference or billing. Dispatch backend behavior,
+dedup, caching, preprocessing and retries execute exactly once as before.
+
+`ExecutionControl.cancel()` and monotonic deadlines are checked before registered
+requests, preprocessing, dispatch and local retry attempts. `ExecutionCancelled`
+derives from BaseException: capture mode and ordinary retry/portfolio failures
+cannot absorb it. Cancellation cannot preempt an in-flight blocking kernel or
+worker; hosts retain process deadlines. Scopes restore on every exit and do not
+implicitly propagate to threads/processes. Nested independent scopes are rejected;
+nested requests preserve their distinct identity and parent linkage.
+
+Managed hosts may opt into `require_scoped_calls=True` on both observation
+scopes. This rejects requests/sampling from unpropagated child threads only while
+the exclusive managed scope is active. Native ToolPool partitions already copy
+ContextVars; native paired MMseqs threads now do likewise. Log-drain, heartbeat,
+progress and standalone process threads do not execute registered public calls.
+Copied scope state is shared and expires on owner exit. Ordinary unobserved use
+and independently scoped non-managed contexts keep their original behavior.
